.TH substroot 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
substroot \- run a command with the root device substituted in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B substroot
.I "command argument ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B substroot
finds the device the root is mounted from, replaces every argument that
is a single
.B %
with that device name, and runs
.IR command .
.PP
It exists so that a boot script can name the root device without knowing
what it is.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# substroot fsck -a %
# substroot remount % ro
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
255 if the root device cannot be found or no command was given;
otherwise whatever the command returns.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prtroot (1),
.BR fsck (1),
.BR remount (1)
